Question 1740
ID
Title Choice of contraception for 33-year-old woman with history of DVT and recent ectopic
pregnancy
Category Obstetrics / Gynecology > Gynecology > Contraception
() Flag as important
FontSiz: A A A
Alison is 33 years old and has come to you for contraception advice. Two years ago, while on
combined oral contraceptive pills (COCP), she developed deep vein thrombosis; therefore, she
was switched to a progestogen-only pill (POP). Last year, she came off the pill to start a family, but
her pregnancy turned out ectopic and aborted six months ago. She wants to begin contraception
again as she is not planning any pregnancies in the near future. Which of the following would be
the correct advice in this regard?','{"A":"She cannot take POP.","B":"She can start taking POP.","C":"She can start taking COCP, but she will need prophylactic anticoagulation.","D":"She can take POP after 12 months of her ectopic pregnancy.","E":"She can start taking COCP."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-3668230cd677","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"dddf00243e788e14ccd7","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":7,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"dddf00243e788e14ccd7","source_file":"Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":7,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Obstetrics","stem":"9:42PM Mon Sep 2\n) Back to MCQs MCQs My Exams\nQuestion 1740\nID\nTitle Choice of contraception for 33-year-old woman with history of DVT and recent ectopic\npregnancy\nCategory Obstetrics / Gynecology > Gynecology > Contraception\n() Flag as important\nFontSiz: A A A\nAlison is 33 years old and has come to you for contraception advice. Two years ago, while on\ncombined oral contraceptive pills (COCP), she developed deep vein thrombosis; therefore, she\nwas switched to a progestogen-only pill (POP). Last year, she came off the pill to start a family, but\nher pregnancy turned out ectopic and aborted six months ago. She wants to begin contraception\nagain as she is not planning any pregnancies in the near futu