her periods, as well as a slight increase in her menstrual flow. She has had this problem since she
started menstruating, and investigations revealed no apparent cause for the presentation.
Recently, she was advised to take combined oral contraceptives (COCs) for both contraception
and treatment of her dysmenorrhea and was started on microgynon 30 mcg. Her dysmenorrhea,
however, persists. Which one of the following would be the next best step in management?','{"A":"Start her on NSAIDs during her menses.","B":"Increase the dose of estrogen.","C":"Decrease the dose of estrogen.","D":"Prescribe progestogen-only pills (POP).","E":"Advise Mirena®."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[15],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-cf7bc1c61f8e","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"005b828c632ea2ad09a7","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":15,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"005b828c632ea2ad09a7","source_file":"Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":15,"supporting_pages":[15],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Obstetrics","stem":"A 29-year-old woman presents to your practice with complaints of annoying pain and cramping with\nher periods, as well as a slight increase in her menstrual flow. She has had this problem since she\nstarted menstruating, and investigations revealed no apparent cause for the presentation.\nRecently, she was advised to take combined oral contraceptives (COCs) for both contraception\nand treatment of her dysmenorrhea and was started on microgynon 30 mcg. Her dysmenorrhea,\nhowever, persists. Which one of the following would be the next best step in management?","options":{"A":"Start her on NSAIDs during her menses.","B":"Increase the dose of estrogen.","C":"Decrease the dose