Question ID 1528
Title Management of intrapartum fetal bradycardia
Category Obstetrics / Gynecology > Obstetrics > Intrauterine fetal surveillance
Flag as unimportant Notes
FontSiz: A A A
Mary, 27 years old, was admitted to the Maternity Ward after her labor pain started. After the
amniotomy, she is placed in the left lateral position and on supplemental oxygen by nasal cannula,
and intravenous fluids and Syntocinon® (oxytocin) infusion are started. A while later and during
fetal heart auscultation, a fetal heart rate (FHR) of 70 bpm is noted. CTG is applied, which reveals
a baseline fetal heart rate of 140 bpm, dropping to 70 bpm periodically with each episode of
bradycardia lasting approximately three minutes. Which one of the following is the most
appropriate next step in management?','{"A":"Fetal scalp blood sampling.","B":"Stop Syntocinon.","C":"Immediate cesarean delivery.","D":"Continuous CTG monitoring.","E":"Reposition to supine."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-ccaf905a64a4","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"3fe0e2113f60efbcc0db","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":31,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"3fe0e2113f60efbcc0db","source_file":"Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":31,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Obstetrics","stem":"9:47PM Mon Sep 2\n> Back to MCQs\nYou''ve flagged this MCQ as important\nMCQs My Exams\nQuestion ID 1528\nTitle Management of intrapartum fetal bradycardia\nCategory Obstetrics / Gynecology > Obstetrics > Intrauterine fetal surveillance\nFlag as unimportant Notes\nFontSiz: A A A\nMary, 27 years old, was admitted to the Maternity Ward after her labor pain started. After the\namniotomy, she is placed in the left lateral position and on supplemental oxygen by nasal cannula,\nand intravenous fluids and Syntocinon® (oxytocin) infusion are started. A while later and during\nfetal heart auscultation, a fetal heart rate (FHR) of 70 bpm is noted. CTG is applied, which reveals\na baseline fetal heart rate of 140 bpm, dropping to 70 bpm periodically with each episode of\nbradycardia lasting approxima