Question ID 1267
Title Management of a CTG abnormality during labor
Category Obstetrics / Gynecology > Obstetrics > Intrauterine fetal surveillance
() Flag as important
A 39-week pregnant woman is admitted to the Labor Unit due to the commencement of labor pain
and contractions. The woman is placed in the left lateral decubitus position and started on
supplemental oxygen and a face mask. An intravenous line is established, and isotonic fluids and
Syntocinon (oxytocin) drip are started according to the protocol. A CTG is performed that shows a
fetal heart rate of 140 which drops to 70 bpm and returns back to the baseline of 140 bpm in
