A 54-year-old woman presents to your clinic with a complaint of a vulvar lesion associated with
severe itching. Her problem started nearly six months ago and has progressed in severity. She has
been menopausal since the age of 50 years. On examination, atrophic white plaques are evident,
as well as excoriation marks over and around the vulva. The labia minora is slightly atrophic, and
there is introitus stenosis. The vaginal examination is normal. The appearance of the vulva is
