Question ID 1202
Title Management of a 13 weeks pregnant woman after exposure to chicken pox
Category Obstetrics / Gynecology > Obstetrics > Perinatal infections
(Flag as important
Robert and Janet are in your clinic for consultation. Robert complains of malaise, mild headache,
and a generalized rash in the form of both intact and unroofed vesicles, as well as macules and
papules. Three weeks ago, Alan, their 7-year-old, was diagnosed with chickenpox. Based on the
history and the appearance of the rash, you make a diagnosis of chickenpox for Robert. Janet is 13
weeks pregnant and is concerned if the infection can affect her and her baby, too. Janet is not sure
if she had chickenpox in childhood. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in the
