A 16-year-old girl who is a dedicated ballet dancer is brought to your clinic by her mother for
evaluation because she has not started menstruation yet. She has a body mass index (BMI) of
16 on examination. Of all secondary sexual characteristics, only breast buds consistent with a
Tanner stage II are present. You order serum FSH, LH, TSH, and prolactin levels, all of which
return normal. Which one of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?','{"A":"Pelvic ultrasonography.","B":"Refer to an adolescent health center.","C":"Reassure that it could be a normal variant of puberty.","D":"Perform a Pap smear.","E":"Karyotyping."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[127],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-b912c3a939d6","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"2d30a7f8b43e625c04a6","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":127,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"2d30a7f8b43e625c04a6","source_file":"Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":127,"supporting_pages":[127],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Obstetrics","stem":",\nA 16-year-old girl who is a dedicated ballet dancer is brought to your clinic by her mother for\nevaluation because she has not started menstruation yet. She has a body mass index (BMI) of\n16 on examination. Of all secondary sexual characteristics, only breast buds consistent with a\nTanner stage II are present. You order serum FSH, LH, TSH, and prolactin levels, all of which\nreturn normal. Which one of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?","options":{"A":"Pelvic ultrasonography.","B":"Refer to an adolescent health center.","C":"Reassure that it could be a normal variant of puberty.","D":"Perform a Pap smear.","E":"Karyotyping."},"source_a