INSERT INTO canonical_records (record_id,source_file,source_page,domain,stem,options_json,source_answer,source_explanation,provenance_json,visual_asset,visual_url,options_mode,current_answer,current_answer_status,current_evidence_json,currentness_risk,record_json,active_quiz,import_version,imported_at) VALUES ('9a5aa0815d06572d329f','Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf','129','Obstetrics','10:08PM Mon Sep 2
a Back to MCQs MCQs My Exams
In hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, the characteristic finding is a decreased serum FSH (and LH). Since
this patient has normal hormonal assays, ultrasonography should be performed for assessment of
possible uterine anomalies or those of the genital tract, resulting in outflow obstruction, some of which
include: Mullerian agenesis, transverse vaginal septum, Asherman''s syndrome, and imperforated
hymen.
One interesting point in the question is that, in fact, with breasts at the Tanner II stage, ultrasound
should have preceded the hormonal assays because, for instance, if this girl was found on ultrasound to
have no uterus, there was no need to measure FSH and other hormones. The diagnostic pathway
should then be continued with karyotyping (option E) and testosterone assays to investigate complete
or incomplete androgen insensitivity as the most likely diagnosis.
Referral to an adolescent health center (option B) may be indicated somewhere down the line once
other causes of primary amenorrhea other than those related to excessive exercise, weight loss, and
eating disorders are excluded with high certainty. It is not appropriate at this stage when other
probable causes of primary amenorrhea are not yet fully investigated.
This girl lags behind normal puberty and cannot be reassured (option C) unless the cause is ensured to
be a constitutional delay of puberty. Interestingly and unlike the common belief, constitutional delay of
puberty is not that common in females compared to males.
Screening with a Pap smear (option D) starts at 25 and is not indicated for this girl now.
TOPIC REVIEW
