Question ID 651
Title Diagnosing the cause of vaginal bleeding in a postmenopausal woman
Category Obstetrics / Gynecology > Gynecology > Disorders of the cervix and uterus
CO Flag as important Notes
A 50-year-old woman presents to your GP practice because of persistent vaginal bleeding for
the last 3 days. Her last menstrual period occurred one year and a half ago. She mentions that
just before the bleeding she felt reduction in hot flushes she has been experiencing for the
past year. She is sexually active and has had regular pap smears with a normal one 6 months
