labor. Her previous pregnancy led to a cesarean section and the delivery of a healthy baby.
The current pregnancy had been uneventful, without any remarkable problems in antenatal
visits except for first-trimester nausea and vomiting. On arrival, she had a cervical dilation of 4
cm, and the fetal head was at -1 station. After five hours, the cervical length and fetal head
station remain the same despite regular uterine contractions. Suddenly, there is a sudden
gush of blood of approximately 1000 mL, and the fetal heart rate drops to 80 bpm on CTG.
