Question ID 642
Title The most likely cause of fetal transverse lie at 37 weeks gestation
Category Obstetrics / Gynecology > Obstetrics > Fetal orientation in utero
(_) Flag as important
On examination of a 28-year-old nulliparous woman at 37 weeks gestation, her fundal height is
found to be 35cm, and her fetus is in a transverse lie. An ultrasound exam in the 18° week
revealed a low-lying placenta. Which one of the following is the most likely cause of this
