Question ID 592
Title Management of a pregnant woman with frontal headache and hypotension
Category Obstetrics / Gynecology > Obstetrics > Medical complications in pregnancy
CO Flag as important Notes
An 18-week pregnant woman is brought to the emergency department with a complaint of
sudden-onset severe frontal headache. On examination, she has a blood pressure of 80/60
mmHg, pulse of 110bpm, respiratory rate of 17 breaths per minute, and temperature of
37.3°C. The rest of the examination is unremarkable. There is no neck stiffness, abdominal
pain or tenderness, or uterine contractions. Which one of the following is the investigation
